\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Relationship between raw spectral radius and reservoir behavior across sign-sweep and shuffle-control families. The top row shows mean task-agnostic performance as a function of raw spectral radius before normalization, \(\rho _{\mathrm  {raw}}\), on a log scale. The bottom row shows the corresponding hyperparameter CV. Columns correspond to GR, IPC, KR, and MC. Lines connect points within experimental families and are not global fitted curves. Across families, lower \(\rho _{\mathrm  {raw}}\) generally coincides with higher performance and higher CV, while higher \(\rho _{\mathrm  {raw}}\) coincides with lower performance and lower CV.}}{10}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:raw_rho_summary}{{6}{10}{Relationship between raw spectral radius and reservoir behavior across sign-sweep and shuffle-control families. The top row shows mean task-agnostic performance as a function of raw spectral radius before normalization, \(\rho _{\mathrm {raw}}\), on a log scale. The bottom row shows the corresponding hyperparameter CV. Columns correspond to GR, IPC, KR, and MC. Lines connect points within experimental families and are not global fitted curves. Across families, lower \(\rho _{\mathrm {raw}}\) generally coincides with higher performance and higher CV, while higher \(\rho _{\mathrm {raw}}\) coincides with lower performance and lower CV}{figure.6}{}}
